# Conventional Commits

Use this subject format for every commit and pull request title:

```
type(optional-scope): subject
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.

- Subject is imperative, lowercase, and has no trailing period.
- Keep the subject within 72 characters.
- A body is optional. When present, it explains why.

```
feat: report scrape freshness on its own endpoint

ci: check Go tests before publishing the image

fix(scrape): fail when the tank name is missing
```

Do not use informal subjects such as `add health` or `still weird`.
